cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Multi-Modal LLM Style Analysis"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Melihov"
    given-names: "Eliran"
  - family-names: "Hanukaiev"
    given-names: "Miron"
abstract: >-
  An unsupervised, zero-shot pipeline for detecting misattributed creations in a
  literary corpus. A large language model extracts a generic style profile from the
  corpus and rewrites every chunk of every text under that profile; the magnitude of
  the required rewrite, measured as a Function-Word Edit Distance, serves as the
  detection signal. The method requires no corpus of comparison authors and no
  classifier training, and produces an interpretable per-creation score.
keywords:
  - stylometry
  - authorship attribution
  - style transfer
  - large language models
  - digital humanities
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/eliranmeleh/Multi-Modal-LLM-Style-Analysis"
